<title>USA: National Semiconductor Q4 earnings summary.</title>
<headline>National Semiconductor Q4 earnings summary.</headline>
<text>
<p>SANTA CLARA, Calif., June 5 (Reuter)</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss primary$0.10	  profit  $0.07</p>
<p> Shr loss diluted0.10	   profit  0.07</p>
<p> Net loss	  14,500	 profit  9,100</p>
<p> Revs		599,200		  612,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary143,400		  137,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted143,400		  137,800</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit	$0.19	  profit  $1.36</p>
<p> Shr profit dil  0.19	   profit  1.34</p>
<p> Net		 27,500		   185,400</p>
<p> Revs		2,507,300		2,623,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary142,600		  132,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted142,900		  138,600</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note - Q4 ended May 25, 1997, includes charges of $87.1 million before tax, or $80.8 million after tax. Net income, excluding the one-time items was $66.3 million, or $0.43 a share. Excluding the effects of the Fairchild businesses, fourth-quarter net income was $61.9 million, or $0.41 a share.</p>
